    "blurb": "The show opens with an acoustic Candyman and a lyric‑improvised Friend Of The Devil, then moves into powerful Black Peter and a seamless Good Lovin' → Turn On Your Lovelight sequence. The other half delivers a soaring The Other One stretch, Cosmic Charlie and solid Pigpen‑style energy.",
    "review": "On April 3 1970 at Cincinnati’s Field House the Dead offered a tightly knit set that blends acoustic intimacy with their trademark electric fire. The show opens with an acoustic Candyman and a lyrical, improvised take on Friend Of The Devil, setting a relaxed tone before launching into a rolling first half that includes Dancin' In The Street, Deep Elem Blues and a standout Black Peter. A rare early‑show acoustic rendition of Wake Up Little Susie finds Jerry and Bob in matching denim, while the mid‑set Good Lovin' → Turn On Your Lovelight sequence drives the energy forward. The second half peaks with a seamless The Other One/Turn On Your Lovelight stretch and a joyous Cosmic Charlie, all underpinned by Phil’s solid bass and the twin drummers’ steady pulse.",
